  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "Let m >= 3 and let G_m be the colored undirected m-cycle whose vertices form one vertex-color class and whose m edges lie in pairwise distinct edge-color classes. If m is odd, then mlt(G_m)=2. In particular mlt(G_5)=2, so the frozen assertion mlt(G_5)=1 in source.md is false. Together with the even case of Proposition 3.26 of arXiv:2609.02382v1, this yields mlt(G_m)=1 for even m and mlt(G_m)=2 for odd m.",
